    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nI occasionally encountered the same issue described in #1774. I followed the [instructions in that issue](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1774#issuecomment-2844928896) to record logs. The changes and logs can be found [here](https://github.com/loichyan/mini.nvim/commit/7201e1b9b67b08bc34134af213f488ce3dcffb2b).\n\nThat said, as mentioned in #1774, this issue is really hard to reproduce. I succeded only 1-2 times out of 10 when testing it myself. According to the log, it seems sometimes `event.completed_item` is set to an empty dict and then mini.completion attempts to show info window with that `event` which contains only one field `completed_item = vim.empty_dict()`.\n\nRaised errors:\n\n```text\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: ...m/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1468: attempt to perform arithmetic on field 'col' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n\t...m/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1468: in function 'info_window_options'\n\t...m/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1373: in function ''\n\tvim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\n```\n\nLogs:\n\n```text\n  }, {\n    col = 33,\n    item = <table 4>,\n    state = \"show_info_window\"\n  }, {\n    col = 6,\n    item = {\n      abbr = \"\",\n      info = \"\",\n      kind = \"\",\n      menu = \"\",\n      user_data = \"\",\n      word = \"loichyan\"\n    },\n    state = \"auto_info\"\n  }, {\n    item = vim.empty_dict(),\n    state = \"auto_info\"\n  }, {\n    item = <5>vim.empty_dict(),\n    state = \"auto_info\"\n  }, {\n    item = <table 5>,\n    state = \"show_info_window\"\n  }, {\n    item = <table 5>,\n    state = \"info_window_options:catch(col=nil)\"\n  }, {\n    item = vim.empty_dict(),\n    state = \"auto_info\"\n  } }\n```\n\nYou can find the full log [here](https://github.com/loichyan/mini.nvim/blob/7201e1b9b67b08bc34134af213f488ce3dcffb2b/_test.log).\n\n### Reproduction\n\nI tried to reproduce this issue with a minimal configuration but failed. However, I did encounter the same issue on both my laptop and my Android tablet. You can view the overall configurations [here](https://github.com/loichyan/nvim/blob/b5c0cfb4538753ade7647936b58758b2d5a2b85a/lua/meowim/plugins/mini/completion.lua).\n\nI also recorded a video of the successful reproduction:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01864ae7-a73c-4054-91c1-9cedb1b0dc1f\n\nThe file I was editing is [this one](https://github.com/loichyan/tmux-toggle-popup/blob/e3f3520ed7b38bdf031d6736cb4f99c6cfc2833d/README.md?plain=1).\n\nFrom my experience, it seems that typing quickly increases the chances of reproducing the issue.",
