            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> The file I was editing is [this one](https://github.com/loichyan/tmux-toggle-popup/blob/e3f3520ed7b38bdf031d6736cb4f99c6cfc2833d/README.md?plain=1).\n\nI noticed that if I type \"lfie\" or \"life\" very quickly in that file, I can almost reproduce this issue every time.\n\nI also recorded logs from extra positions. Here are the newly updated logs, along with some guesses about the cause of the issue:\n\n```lua\n{ {\n    -- First, the complete item \"loichyan\" is triggered by the first letter \"l\".\n    item = <1>{\n      abbr = \"\",\n      info = \"\",\n      kind = \"\",\n      menu = \"\",\n      user_data = \"\",\n      word = \"loichyan\"\n    },\n    state = \"auto_info:enter\"\n  }, {\n    -- Then a `show_info_window` call is scheduled.\n    item = <table 1>,\n    state = \"auto_info:show_info_window\"\n  }, {\n    -- Right after the above `CompleteChanged` event, another event is fired\n    -- with an empty dict as its only field `completed_item`.\n    item = <2>vim.empty_dict(),\n    state = \"auto_info:enter\"\n  }, {\n    -- `auto_info` observes this and decides to close the action window.\n    -- I haven't figured out what this function does yet, but it does not\n    -- cancel the previous `show_info_window` call, which seems expected here.\n    item = <table 2>,\n    state = \"auto_info:close_action_window\"\n  }, {\n    -- Then mini.completion enters `show_info_window`, but the event has\n    -- been overridden with an invalid `event` table.\n    item = <table 2>,\n    state = \"show_info_window:enter\"\n  }, {\n    item = <table 2>,\n    state = \"info_window_options:catch(col=nil)\"\n  }, {\n    item = <3>vim.empty_dict(),\n    state = \"auto_info:enter\"\n  }, {\n    item = <table 3>,\n    state = \"auto_info:close_action_window\"\n  }, {\n    item = <4>vim.empty_dict(),\n    state = \"auto_info:enter\"\n  }, {\n    item = <table 4>,\n    state = \"auto_info:close_action_window\"\n  } }\n```\n\nYou can view the changes and logs [here](https://github.com/loichyan/mini.nvim/commit/b81c69f7e676a8b914bc10872098831d5faf0ed5). Hope this could help!\n",
