            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Hello o/\n\nI did indeed reproduce this issue with a minimal conf:\n\n```lua\n-- 'noinsert' selects the first item each time the completion menu appears, \n-- triggering the info window.\nvim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,noinsert,fuzzy'\nrequire('mini.completion').setup({\n  -- This configuration may not be critical, \n  -- but it increases the likelihood of reproducing this issue.\n  delay = { completion = 50, info = 0 },\n})\n\n```\n\nHere is a screencast:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4a1a4f1f-abb4-48ee-b7be-787382ba159b\n\nI also wrote a helper script to simulate fast typing, and you can follow these steps to reproduce:\n\n1. Open tmux with two panes\n2. In the left pane, open README.md of mini.nvim in Neovim\n3. Go to the right pane, then run the script `./_do_test.sh`\n4. Find out which delay most triggers the error\n5. Re-run the script with that delay\n\nYou can find all the changes, logs and scripts [here](https://github.com/loichyan/mini.nvim/commit/50c2503b054fbae3a5835764926f1e928a9f11ff).\n\nIn conclusion, my configurations appear to only increase the chances of reproducing this issue, as they load bunch of plugins and add typing latency. I also found the most likely culprit ([link](https://github.com/loichyan/mini.nvim/blob/48f48e4b3f317e9da34ee7a01958b4c5018e2d34/lua/mini/completion.lua#L911)):\n\n```lua\n  local win_id = H.info.win_id\n  if H.is_valid_win(win_id) and delay > 0 then\n    vim.wo[win_id].winhighlight = vim.wo[win_id].winhighlight .. ',FloatBorder:MiniCompletionInfoBorderOutdated'\n  end\n  H.info.timer:start(delay, 0, vim.schedule_wrap(H.show_info_window))\n  --                               ^ this schedule call\n```\n\nSo, here is my guess why this issue occurs:\n\n```lua\n{ {\n    -- 1) A valid complete item triggers `show_info_window`\n    item = <1>{\n      abbr = \"\",\n      info = \"\",\n      kind = \"\",\n      menu = \"\",\n      user_data = \"\",\n      word = \"for\"\n    },\n    state = \"auto_info:enter\"\n  }, {\n    item = <table 1>,\n    state = \"auto_info:show_info_window\"\n  }, {\n    -- 2) The `info.timer` ends and calls `schedule_wrap(show_info_window)`.\n    -- However, `show_info_window` is not invoked immediately as it is scheduled.\n    -- Note: I changed it to `schedule(fun() ... end)` here to log the state.\n    item = <table 1>,\n    state = \"auto_info:schedule(show_info_window)\"\n  }, {\n    -- 3) Later, another `CompleteChanged` event is fired before entering `show_info_window`.\n    -- This time, the complete item is invalid and overrides the previous one.\n    item = <2>vim.empty_dict(),\n    state = \"auto_info:enter\"\n  }, {\n    item = <table 2>,\n    state = \"auto_info:close_action_window\"\n  }, {\n    -- 4) Finally, we enter `show_info_window`, but the complete item has become\n    -- invalid, which causes an error immediately.\n    item = <table 2>,\n    state = \"show_info_window:enter\"\n  }, {\n    item = <table 2>,\n    state = \"info_window_options:catch(col=nil)\"\n  }, {\n    item = <3>vim.empty_dict(),\n  },\n```\n",
