        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "So I did manage to reproduce with custom Lua config (don't really use `tmux`):\n\n```lua\nvim.o.completeopt = 'menuone,noinsert,fuzzy'\nvim.o.cmdheight = 25\nrequire('mini.completion').setup({\n  delay = { completion = 50, info = 0 },\n})\n\nlocal words = 'jakld lfi judakljc pluwlkcjawkl lif gux priencx eho12 da23x'\nlocal n_char, delay = 0, 51\n_G.type_text = function()\n  if vim.fn.mode() ~= 'i' then\n    n_char = 0\n    vim.api.nvim_input('cc')\n  end\n\n  n_char = n_char + 1\n  local char = words:sub(n_char, n_char)\n  if char == '' then return end\n  vim.api.nvim_input(char)\n  vim.defer_fn(_G.type_text, delay)\nend\n```\n\nThe reason indeed seems to be a not properly cancelled showing of info window when there is no LSP server attached. I'll fix it.\n\nAlso, one of the reasons why I couldn't reproduce is because it might require `noinsert` instead of `noselect` to be reproduced more reliably, which I missed.",
            "created_at": "2025-07-10T15:04:26Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1890#issuecomment-3057846451",
            "id": 3057846451,
